												<div class=3D"subSection detailBox" id=3D"7788499">
							<div class=3D"subSectionTitle">
								1 - About the HSB and thumbnails																<span class=3D"subS=
ectionEditLink"><a href=3D"https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/editguide=
subsection/?id=3D3445083893&amp;sectionid=3D7788499">Edit</a></span>
															</div>
							<div class=3D"subSectionDesc">
								Some information about the <b>HSB</b> and map preview thumbnails:<b=
r><ul class=3D"bb_ul"><li> This is the screen you see when you first enter =
the game, showing thumbnail preview images of different maps running on ava=
ilable game-servers.  Because of its visual nature (images), this is referr=
ed-to as the <b><u>Highlighted</u> Server Browser</b> (or <b>HSB</b>).<br><=
a href=3D"https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/36697142552416671/A67FA8B=
B5AF9B5EA1027E36A2F7B7834B89C5684/" class=3D"modalContentLink" data-modal-c=
ontent-popup-url=3D"https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/displayimageform=
odaldialog/?imageurl=3Dhttps%3A%2F%2Fimages.steamusercontent.com%2Fugc%2F36=
697142552416671%2FA67FA8BB5AF9B5EA1027E36A2F7B7834B89C5684%2F"><img src=3D"=
https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/36697142552416671/A67FA8BB5AF9B5EA1=
027E36A2F7B7834B89C5684/" class=3D"sharedFilePreviewImage sizeFull" alt=3D"=
" title=3D""></a></li><li> This feature is how most <a class=3D"bb_link" hr=
ef=3D"https://store.steampowered.com/app/265630/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"=
">Fistful of Frags</a> (<b>FoF</b>) players find and connect to servers to =
play the game.  This is <i>especially</i> true for those new to the game.<b=
r></li><li> Having a map preview thumbnail shown is <i>extremely helpful</i=
> to players, who may only recognize maps by what they look-like visually. =
 Also the <b>HSB</b>, does not by itself show the <b>name</b> of the map cu=
rrently being run by the server - only a <u>matching</u> preview thumbnail =
or the generic "Custom Map" icon.<br></li><li> Unfortunately, <b>FoF</b> cu=
rrently only includes preview thumbnails for maps that shipped with the gam=
e at the time of its last update - nearly <b>two</b> (<b>2</b>) years ago. =
 So no preview thumbnails are included for any custom maps released by the =
community - resulting in the generic "<b>Custom Map</b>" icon being shown i=
nstead of an actual map preview.<br></li><li> Ideally map authors, would cr=
eate preview thumbnails for the maps and include them when they distribute =
the maps.  However, many (mostly really) map authors are currently unfamili=
ar with this process, in part because (as far as I can determine) its not w=
ell documented.  Also, many custom / community maps pre-date the existence =
of the <b>HSB</b> feature entirely.<br></li><li> That's correct, the HSB <i=
>did not even exist</i> in earlier releases of <b>FoF</b>.<br></li><li> Thi=
s guide aims to remedy that situation - for both <b>map authors</b> <i>crea=
ting</i> new maps for <b>FoF</b>, as well as for <b>server operators</b> <i=
>hosting</i> community maps on their <b>FoF</b> game-servers.</li></ul>				=
				<div style=3D"clear: both"></div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div style=3D"clear: both"></div>
												<div class=3D"subSection detailBox" id=3D"7788505">
							<div class=3D"subSectionTitle">
								2 - Prerequisites (things you need first)																<span clas=
s=3D"subSectionEditLink"><a href=3D"https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/=
editguidesubsection/?id=3D3445083893&amp;sectionid=3D7788505">Edit</a></spa=
n>
															</div>
							<div class=3D"subSectionDesc">
								Some things you will need (assuming you are doing this on <b>Window=
s</b>) are:<br><ul class=3D"bb_ul"><li> <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https:=
//store.steampowered.com/app/265630/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">Fistful of=
 Frags</a> already installed.<br></li><li> Whichever <b>map</b> (you are ma=
king a thumbnail for) installed in the <b>fof/maps</b> sub-folder.<br></li>=
<li> <b>Any text editor</b>. For these examples, <b>Windows Notepad</b> wil=
l be used - since it is widely available.<br></li><li> <b><a class=3D"bb_li=
nk" href=3D"http://paint.net/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">Paint.NE=
T</a></b> - available <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://www.getpaint.net=
/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">here</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host"=
>[www.getpaint.net]</span>.  You may actually use any imaged editor <i>with=
 equivalent features</i>.  Unfortunately, <b>Windows Paint</b> will <i>not<=
/i> easily suffice.<br></li><li> <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://githu=
b.com/NeilJed/VTFLib/releases/tag/1.3.2" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener=
">VTFEdit</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host">[github.com]</span> for convertin=
g the image file into Valve's proprietary <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"http=
s://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/VTF_(Valve_Texture_Format)" target=3D"=
_blank" rel=3D"">VTF</a> texture format (more info <a class=3D"bb_link" hre=
f=3D"https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/VTFEdit" target=3D"_blank" re=
l=3D"">here</a>)<br></li><li> <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"http://www.riint=
ouge.com/VIDE/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">VIDE</a><span class=3D"=
bb_link_host">[www.riintouge.com]</span> for manipulating the map BSP file =
(more info <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://developer.valvesoftware.com=
/wiki/VIDE" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">here</a>)<br></li><li> <a class=3D"b=
b_link" href=3D"https://www.7-zip.org/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener"=
>7-Zip</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host">[www.7-zip.org]</span> for various f=
ile/folder compression tasks.</li></ul><b><u>Note</u>:</b> For those wishin=
g to do this on <b>Linux</b> (<a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://linuxmin=
t.com/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">Linux Mint</a><span class=3D"bb=
_link_host">[linuxmint.com]</span> being my personal favorite for desktop L=
inux installations), the key <i>differences</i> and your key <i>equivalents=
</i> are probably:<br><ul class=3D"bb_ul"><li> Obviously, the <b>paths</b> =
for everything will be <i>different</i>, and the <b>screens</b> will <i>not=
 look the same</i>.<br></li><li> Whatever default <b>text-editor</b> comes =
with your Linux distribution.<br></li><li> Whatever <b>image editor</b> you=
 prefer (<a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://www.pinta-project.com/" targe=
t=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">Pinta</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host">[www.p=
inta-project.com]</span>, <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://www.gimp.org=
/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">Gimp</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host"=
>[www.gimp.org]</span>, etc.).<br></li><li> <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"ht=
tp://www.riintouge.com/VIDE/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">VIDE</a><=
span class=3D"bb_link_host">[www.riintouge.com]</span> is actually availabl=
e for Linux also! (although, I have not tried it myself).<br></li><li> <a c=
lass=3D"bb_link" href=3D"http://www.riintouge.com/VIDE/" target=3D"_blank" =
rel=3D" noopener">VIDE</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host">[www.riintouge.com]<=
/span> has a built-in function similar to <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"http=
s://github.com/NeilJed/VTFLib/releases/tag/1.3.2" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"=
 noopener">VTFEdit</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host">[github.com]</span> that=
 should suffice (although, I have not tried it myself).</li></ul><br>						=
		<div style=3D"clear: both"></div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div style=3D"clear: both"></div>
												<div class=3D"subSection detailBox" id=3D"7788509">
							<div class=3D"subSectionTitle">
								3 - Capturing a screenshot to use																<span class=3D"sub=
SectionEditLink"><a href=3D"https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/editguid=
esubsection/?id=3D3445083893&amp;sectionid=3D7788509">Edit</a></span>
															</div>
							<div class=3D"subSectionDesc">
								Generally, it is best practice to base the map preview thumbnail on=
 a screenshot of the map, in order to best present what that map looks like=
 to the player.   However, <i>if you are the map author</i>, alternative op=
tion might be to create some <i>artistic representation</i> of the map - if=
 you feel that would better represent the map.  For the purposes of this gu=
ide, I will use a screenshot as the basis for the preview thumbnail.<br><br=
><div class=3D"bb_h1">Overall process:</div><br>At a high-level the part of=
 the process is:<br><ul class=3D"bb_ul"><li> Launch <a class=3D"bb_link" hr=
ef=3D"https://store.steampowered.com/app/265630" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D""=
>Fistful of Frags</a> (<b>FoF</b>).<br></li><li> Make sure the "developer c=
onsole" is <b>enabled</b>.  <i>If you are not sure how to do this</i>, see =
the notes and image below for how to do this.<br></li><li> Start a game usi=
ng the <b>map</b> you wish to create a preview thumbnail for.  Be sure that=
 you also configure the game for the appropriate <b>FoF</b> <i>game-mode</i=
> the map requires.  <i>If you are not sure how to do this</i>, see the not=
es and image below for how to do this.<br></li><li> If you have <b>net_grap=
h</b> enabled, <i>turn it off</i> (e.g. set <b>net_graph 0</b>).<br></li><l=
i> Switch to spectator mode (e.g. change to the <b>Spectator</b> team).<br>=
</li><li> Move around in spectator mode until you have a good point-of-view=
 on-screen the best represents what this map is like (and that players will=
 later recognize it as).<br></li><li> Capture a screenshot, and save it to =
a file you can edit.</li></ul><hr><br><div class=3D"bb_h1">Enabling the "De=
veloper Console":</div><ul class=3D"bb_ul"><li> Open the <b>options</b> men=
u, by clicking the <b>gear-shaped</b> icon the left-side of the screen.<br>=
</li><li> Make sure you have the "<b>Keyboard</b>" tab selected/shown.<br><=
/li><li> Click the "<b>Advanced</b>" button.<br></li><li> Ensure that the "=
<b>Enable developer console</b>" option is selected/checked.<br></li><li> C=
lick the "<b>Ok</b>" button to close that dialog.<br></li><li> Be aware tha=
t (by default) you toggle the developer console open and closed using the <=
b>tilde</b> ("<b>~</b>") key.  You can also re-map this to another key if y=
ou desire.  It is listed in the <b>Keyboard</b> tab as "toggle console".<br=
></li><li> If you are done making changes, click the "<b>Ok</b>" on the opt=
ions dialog to close that screen.</li></ul><a href=3D"https://images.steamu=
sercontent.com/ugc/36697142552687467/C7DF7562C8C79D1D7A9821B748EB87311AE878=
5A/" class=3D"modalContentLink" data-modal-content-popup-url=3D"https://ste=
amcommunity.com/sharedfiles/displayimageformodaldialog/?imageurl=3Dhttps%3A=
%2F%2Fimages.steamusercontent.com%2Fugc%2F36697142552687467%2FC7DF7562C8C79=
D1D7A9821B748EB87311AE8785A%2F"><img src=3D"https://images.steamusercontent=
.com/ugc/36697142552687467/C7DF7562C8C79D1D7A9821B748EB87311AE8785A/" class=
=3D"sharedFilePreviewImage sizeFull" alt=3D"" title=3D""></a><hr><br><div c=
lass=3D"bb_h1">Starting a game (locally) with the desired map:</div><ul cla=
ss=3D"bb_ul"><li> Launch <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://store.steampo=
wered.com/app/265630" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">Fistful of Frags</a> (<b>F=
oF</b>).<br></li><li> Press the <b>tilde</b> ("<b>~</b>") key - or whicheve=
r key you have "toggle console" bound-to.<br></li><li> The <b>developer con=
sole</b> window should open.<br></li><li> This <b>developer console</b> is =
essentially a <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Co=
mmand-line_interface" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">command-line inte=
rface</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host">[en.wikipedia.org]</span> - where you=
 can enter various text-based commands, one-line at a time.<br></li><li> Se=
t the <b>fof_sv_currentmode</b> <i>console variable</i> (or <b>CVAR</b>) to=
 the mode that the map is compatible with.<br></li><li> For example, enter =
this command and press <b>ENTER</b> to set the game for <b>FoF</b> "Shoot-O=
ut" mode (used by maps with names starting with "<b>fof_</b>":<br><div clas=
s=3D"bb_code">fof_sv_currentmode 1</div></li><li> Alternatively, enter this=
 command and press <b>ENTER</b> to set the game for <b>FoF</b> "Team-Play" =
mode (used by maps with names starting with "<b>tp_</b>":<br><div class=3D"=
bb_code">fof_sv_currentmode 2</div></li><li> The full list of possible game=
-modes are:<br><div class=3D"bb_code">1 =3D Deathmatch and/or Team-Deathmat=
ch
2 =3D Team-based Objectives, Zone-Capture, etc.
3 =3D Break Bad
4 =3D Elimination
5 =3D Versus
6 =3D Cooperative</div></li><li> The command to start the game (using the m=
ap of your choice), is the <i>not-ironically-named</i> "<b>map</b>" command=
.  Simply enter "<b>map</b>", followed by a space, then the name of the map=
 you want to start, and then press <b>ENTER</b>.  For example:<br><div clas=
s=3D"bb_code">map fof_cripplecreek</div></li></ul><hr><br><div class=3D"bb_=
h1">Capturing a screenshot:</div>Move around the map in <b>FoF</b> in "spec=
tator" mode, and find point-of-view that you think would best show most to =
a player <i>which</i> map this is - for them to <i>recognize</i> it easily =
later.<br><br><u>Using <b>Steam</b>'s screenshot feature</u>:<br><ul class=
=3D"bb_ul"><li> Use whatever hot-key you have setup for Steam's screenshot =
function.  The default if <b>F12</b>.<br></li><li> Close <b>FoF</b>.<br></l=
i><li> <i>Right-click</i> on the Steam icon in the bottom-right corner of t=
he Windows task-bar.<br></li><li> Select the <b>Screenshots</b> option.<br>=
</li><li> Browse through the recent screenshot and click on the one you wan=
t to use.<br></li><li> <i>Right-click</i> on the image, and select the <b>C=
opy to clipboard</b> option.<br></li><li> Open your image editor (<b><a cla=
ss=3D"bb_link" href=3D"http://paint.net/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopene=
r">Paint.NET</a></b> or whatever editor you are using) and paste the clipbo=
ard contents into it.<br></li><li> Save a copy of the image somewhere you c=
an find it easily.</li></ul><br><br><br>								<div style=3D"clear: both">=
