							<div class=3D"subSectionDesc">
								As map authors for <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://store.steam=
powered.com/app/265630" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">Fistful of Frags</a> and=
/or other <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://developer.valvesoftware.com/=
wiki/Source" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">Source</a>-engine games are likely =
already aware, there are often <i>additional</i> files associated with a ma=
p - which should be <i>distributed with it</i>.<br><br>Commonly, these migh=
t be:<br><ul class=3D"bb_ul"><li> <i>Navigation</i> files (<b>.nav</b>) - f=
or servers hosting the map (or players running it locally) to be able to us=
e in-game "bots".<br></li><li> <i>Readme</i> type text files (<b>.txt</b>) =
- to provide additional information to players.<br></li><li> <i>Configurati=
on</i> files (<b>.cfg</b>) - for servers hosting the map.<br></li><li> Cust=
om <i>sound</i> files (<b>.mp3</b> and/or <b>.wav</b>) that the map require=
s.<br></li><li> Custom <i>3d model</i> files (<b>.mdl</b>) that the map req=
uires.<br></li><li> Custom <i>texture</i> files (<b>.vtf</b> and <b>.vmt</b=
>) that the map requires - <i>including</i> map preview thumbnail textures =
for the  <b>HSB</b> feature of <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://store.s=
teampowered.com/app/265630/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">Fistful of Frags</a=
> (the reason for <b><i>this guide</i></b>)!</li></ul>There are several way=
s to ensure that these files are kept with the map when it is distributed. =
 There is a bit of history here with different methods - which it is worth =
knowing because <i>different</i> or even <i>multiple</i> techniques may be =
used in different <i>circumstances</i>.  Allowing for variations, the <b>fo=
ur</b> (<b>4</b>) most common methods are:<br><ol><li> Using a map-specific=
 <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Reso=
urce_list_(Source)" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">resource list</a> - typicall=
y used when distributing the map as a zipped-archive (<b>.zip</b>) file.  T=
his is the oldest technique, and pre-dates the <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D=
"https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Source" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"=
">Source</a> engine entirely, dating back to the prior <a class=3D"bb_link"=
 href=3D"https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/GoldSrc" target=3D"_blank=
" rel=3D"">GoldSrc</a> engine - <i>possibly</i> even further to some versio=
n of the <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quake_e=
ngine" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">Quake</a><span class=3D"bb_link_=
host">[en.wikipedia.org]</span> engine.  <i>Game-servers</i> still often us=
e this technique to work-around custom maps that do not already have everyt=
hing <i>embedded</i>.<br></li><li> Embedding everything directly into the m=
ap's <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/=
BSP_(Source)" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">BSP</a> file. To a limited extent,=
 this also pre-dates the <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://developer.val=
vesoftware.com/wiki/Source" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">Source</a> engine, d=
ating back to the prior <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://developer.valv=
esoftware.com/wiki/GoldSrc" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">GoldSrc</a> engine. =
 Although it has now become the very-much <i>preferred/standard practice</i=
> for distributing any map that requires other files <i>that are not part o=
f the base game installation</i> (i.e. "custom" files) - in particular rega=
rding custom <b>sounds</b>, <b>models</b> and/or <b>textures</b>.<br></li><=
li> Packaging everything in a <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https://develope=
r.valvesoftware.com/wiki/VPK" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">VPK</a> file.  Thi=
s newest method has become common, since the advent of the <a class=3D"bb_l=
ink" href=3D"https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Steam_Workshop" targe=
t=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">Steam Workshop</a>.  It accomplishes something simila=
r to embedding directly into the map's <a class=3D"bb_link" href=3D"https:/=
/developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/BSP_(Source)" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"">=
BSP</a> file, without some of the downsides.  However, it has its own downs=
ides for servers hosting custom maps.<br></li><li> For <i>server operators<=
/i>, using a 3rd-party server-side modifications (such as <a class=3D"bb_li=
nk" href=3D"http://sourcemod.net/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D" noopener">Sour=
ceMod</a><span class=3D"bb_link_host">[sourcemod.net]</span>) to download t=
he files to players as they connect to the server to play the map.  This la=
st method, is typically used by server operators to work-around existing ma=
ps that require related files but <i>do not include them already <b>embedde=
d</b></i>, or to download files that apply to <i>multiple</i> maps - or are=
 associated with custom server-side plug-ins.</li></ol>Each of these method=
s is discussed in more detail, in the sections that follow.<br>								<div=
